<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhang Shicheng</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1321–<a href="/years/1367">1367</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhang Shicheng was a salt-boat worker who rose in revolt against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a> in 1353 and set up the state of Zhou, ruling the rich <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangtze-river">Yangtze</a> delta from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suzhou">Suzhou</a>. He wavered between rebellion and Yuan allegiance, and his troops killed the Red Turban leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-futong">Liu Futong</a> in 1363. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hongwu-emperor">Zhu Yuanzhang</a> besieged Suzhou and captured him in 1367, and he took his own life soon after.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zhang-shicheng.jpg" alt="Zhang Shicheng" width="254" height="352" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ZhangShicheng.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
